Z||000001||Carrolles||03-27-2001||06:49 PM||||A past issue of Popular Machanics said that the 2002 model will be the last.  Don't know for sure though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||03-27-2001||07:05 PM||||Everything I've heard says 2002 will be the last model year.  Some car mags are also saying they've heard of plans for a "swan song" T/A and Z28 with the Z06 Corvette's LS6!  Sure to be overpriced and unobtainable by mortals.  More rumours speculate that the Chevy SSR sport truck will replace the Camaro, while the Opel Speedster (or an Americanized version) will either replace the Firebird or fill the void till something else comes along.  Also, I've heard GM is cancelling production for a complete redesign and the F-body will return in 2004 or 2005 with retro styling reminiscant of the 69's (it's worked for Chrysler, maybe it'll work for The General).  Any or all of this could be bunk or truth.  Who knows?  I'm very confident that the Fbody goes away in 2002 and the SSR will be produced.  Everything else is speculation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||03-27-2001||07:11 PM||||St terese (spelling) plant here in Canada where the cars are built is scheduled to be re tooled and shut down for a while in late 2002, There is going to be no Z06 F body this froma friend who works in marketing @ GM's head office in detroit , along with that no V8 front drive impala.<P>There were rumors of a Front drive camaro , but thank god it is being killed and not tortured... Remember when Ford intro duced the Probe?? That was suppsoe to be the new mustang.. haha I have pics around here somewhere my uncle gave me (owns an ford dealership) of a mustang badged probe...<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||SWTKSTMS||03-27-2001||07:51 PM||||the last i heard about the camaro is that 2002 or 2003 is going to be the last production year for the camaros. also that the ssr will replace it. but that was about three months ago, so who knows what has changed||||reg||1
